1
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Ouch!

2
00:01:33,170 --> 00:01:34,170
Good morning.

3
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:38,860
Smells so good.

4
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:51,140
Isn't it a hassle to make
pour-over coffee every time?

5
00:01:52,610 --> 00:01:55,810
How about I buy you a
coffee maker to cover my rent?

6
00:01:56,900 --> 00:02:00,770
No thanks, I like doing it this way.

7
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:07,220
More importantly,

8
00:02:08,640 --> 00:02:10,240
don't just crawl into my bed.

9
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:13,400
It's a double bed anyway,
what's the big deal?

10
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:15,720
That's not the point.

11
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:18,980
What's this?

12
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:23,590
Got it on sale for cheap.

13
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:28,360
And here you are, doing
the exact same thing.

14
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:30,120
Shut up.

15
00:02:32,270 --> 00:02:35,500
I heard it's really soothing,
or rather, great for stress relief.

16
00:02:46,250 --> 00:02:47,250
Kanda.

17
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:51,740
Seriously, stop crawling into my bed.

18
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:59,520
Get up! We're gonna be late.

19
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:00,960
Hmm...

20
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:11,850
Ueno, can I go to work with you today?

21
00:03:15,340 --> 00:03:16,340
Are you serious?

22
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:19,530
Some people at work know I'm gay.

23
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:22,020
Didn't I tell you not to talk
to me so much at the office?

24
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:24,520
Yeah, yeah.

25
00:03:24,830 --> 00:03:27,400
Still, we can at least take
the train together, right?

26
00:04:27,140 --> 00:04:29,560
"You Should Be The One To Come Kiss Me"

27
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:31,729
(Episode 2)

28
00:04:31,730 --> 00:04:33,530
A Sales Department dinner?

29
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:34,860
Yes...

30
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:37,820
It's next Monday.

31
00:04:39,100 --> 00:04:40,260
Would you be able to make it?

32
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:42,640
Is it okay for me to go,
since I'm in Accounting?

33
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:46,110
It's also to celebrate
Sales landing a big client.

34
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:49,680
We're inviting people from other
departments too, so if you're free...

35
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,500
There's still a miscalculation here.

36
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:54,990
Sorry.

37
00:04:58,710 --> 00:04:59,950
I appreciate the invite, but...

38
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,040
Oh.

39
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:04,960
It's a team appreciation dinner,
so it's on the company, of course.

40
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:06,180
I'm in.

41
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:12,460
I'm back.

42
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:13,960
Good work, everyone.

43
00:05:14,980 --> 00:05:16,959
Shirai, is the proposal ready?

44
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:17,960
All done.

45
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:19,800
Oh, thanks.

46
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:23,580
I invited Ueno-san to the dinner, too.

47
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:26,376
He said yes the second you
mentioned it's on the company, right?

48
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:28,280
Yep! Worked like a charm.

49
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:29,440
Told you.

50
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:36,050
Are you and Ueno-san close, Kanda-san?

51
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:38,530
Yeah.

52
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:44,920
Didn't I tell you not to talk
to me so much at the office?

53
00:05:46,050 --> 00:05:47,450
I wouldn't say we're on good terms.

54
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:48,700
Well, which is it?

55
00:05:58,230 --> 00:05:59,500
About Ueno-san...

56
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:03,280
Hmm?

57
00:06:05,980 --> 00:06:06,980
Never mind.

58
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:09,460
There are rumors that
you two don't get along,

59
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:12,520
so I was just curious which one was true.

60
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:15,250
Huh? People are saying that?

61
00:06:18,670 --> 00:06:19,920
Forget I said anything.

62
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:22,980
Too late for that.

63
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:24,590
Now it's gonna bug me.

64
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:25,880
- Shirai.
- Yes?

65
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:27,606
- Kobayashi?
- You just bumped into me.

66
00:06:27,630 --> 00:06:29,380
Hold on a sec, Shirai.

67
00:06:40,770 --> 00:06:42,210
Are you having lunch here too, Ueno?

68
00:06:46,060 --> 00:06:48,940
Would you be happy getting puffed
corn snacks and dried squid as a gift?

69
00:06:50,780 --> 00:06:51,780
Sure.

70
00:06:52,060 --> 00:06:53,480
Those corn snacks are pretty good.

71
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:57,360
Even as a promotion gift for a friend?

72
00:06:58,220 --> 00:06:59,220
What?

73
00:06:59,320 --> 00:07:01,400
Then you should definitely
get them something nicer.

74
00:07:04,290 --> 00:07:05,830
He's the one who asked for it.

75
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:10,480
What is he, a high schooler?

76
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:14,670
Isn't it best to just
get him what he wants?

77
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:16,260
True.

78
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:19,883
Getting something that isn't aligned
with your taste can be kind of a pain.

79
00:07:26,223 --> 00:07:27,240
What's wrong?

80
00:08:06,730 --> 00:08:10,450
Any updates on that wish list?

81
00:08:15,420 --> 00:08:18,260
Please let me know if there's any progress.

82
00:08:36,260 --> 00:08:37,360
Congrats.

83
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:44,520
Huh?

84
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:46,980
Don't tell me you're
trying to brush this off.

85
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:51,530
Maybe.

86
00:08:58,860 --> 00:09:01,490
Are you limiting yourself to
one-word replies or something?

87
00:09:07,330 --> 00:09:08,500
Annoying.

88
00:09:58,340 --> 00:09:59,340
Welcome.

89
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:14,060
Are you looking for a tie?

90
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Um...

91
00:10:22,490 --> 00:10:24,030
I'm buying one for a friend.

92
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,810
Would it be weird to give a tie as a gift?

93
00:10:27,180 --> 00:10:29,060
No, not at all.

94
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:33,710
Many customers buy them to
celebrate promotions or birthdays.

95
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:35,980
I see...

96
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:37,080
Yes.

97
00:10:50,350 --> 00:10:52,019
Let's pool our strength together

98
00:10:52,043 --> 00:10:54,383
and take on even greater challenges.

99
00:10:58,380 --> 00:11:00,569
Now, let's have the project leader,

100
00:11:00,570 --> 00:11:03,800
Kanda-san from Sales, say a
few words and lead the toast.

101
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:07,620
Thank you.

102
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,820
Thank you for the introduction.
I'm Kanda from the Sales Department.

103
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:14,080
Just as Department
Manager Tabata mentioned,

104
00:11:14,290 --> 00:11:16,720
the real test for this project starts now.

105
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:19,550
With everyone's help, I hope we can

106
00:11:19,630 --> 00:11:23,250
- build new relationships of trust...
- Ueno, you made it.

107
00:11:23,470 --> 00:11:24,560
Thank goodness.

108
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:26,480
I'm the only one here from PR.

109
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:27,960
Same for me from Accounting.

110
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:30,830
We're kind of out of place here, huh?

111
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:38,880
Looking for someone?

112
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:39,920
Nope.

113
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:43,250
Isn't Kanda dragging this out a bit?

114
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:45,380
He literally just started.

115
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:55,040
I think I'll go grab a drink, too.

116
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:04,550
Excuse me...

117
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:07,170
Sorry, can I order a drink right now?

118
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:08,800
Here.

119
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:11,040
Oolong tea, right?

120
00:12:14,610 --> 00:12:15,390
Thanks.

121
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:18,200
I look forward to working with
you all and appreciate your support.

122
00:12:18,300 --> 00:12:20,810
That said, if I keep
talking business like this,

123
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:23,070
the manager might chew me out,

124
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:26,840
so I'll wrap it up here.

125
00:12:28,060 --> 00:12:30,360
Does everyone have a drink?

126
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:34,040
By the way, we have people from
other departments joining us tonight,

127
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:36,690
so let's use this chance to mingle...

128
00:12:38,340 --> 00:12:39,340
All right.

129
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:41,010
I know that was a bit short,

130
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:45,580
but it sounds like Shirai is starving.

131
00:12:45,780 --> 00:12:46,960
Did everyone hear that?

132
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:48,580
All right, let's do the toast!

133
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:50,840
Glasses up, everyone.

134
00:12:51,560 --> 00:12:52,560
Here we go.

135
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:55,560
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

136
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:58,180
Thank you.

137
00:12:58,980 --> 00:12:59,980
Thanks.

138
00:13:00,110 --> 00:13:01,780
Great job.

139
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:11,290
- You've been working really hard.
- It's all thanks to you, boss.

140
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:12,699
Sorry to always trouble you.

141
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:14,180
Let's not talk about work at a party.

142
00:13:14,420 --> 00:13:15,520
I'm really sorry.

143
00:13:15,593 --> 00:13:17,772
Still, the deadline's tomorrow,
so I'm counting on you.

144
00:13:17,822 --> 00:13:18,563
Tomorrow?

145
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,920
Want to grab a drink together sometime?

146
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:24,520
We haven't gone out
for drinks yet, have we?

147
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:26,640
Right?

148
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:28,900
Are you listening?

149
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:29,900
To what I just said.

150
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:31,520
Are you even listening to me?

151
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:32,500
Yeah, I'm listening.

152
00:13:32,501 --> 00:13:33,700
Good, good.

153
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:35,400
Sorry for the wait.

154
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,230
Great, thank you.

155
00:13:39,660 --> 00:13:40,860
Whoa, what's up with you?

156
00:13:41,100 --> 00:13:42,340
Oh, you're here too, Mizoguchi.

157
00:13:46,740 --> 00:13:47,740
Are you okay?

158
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:49,280
Is that alcohol?

159
00:13:49,910 --> 00:13:51,330
No, it's oolong tea...

160
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:54,560
Hey!

161
00:13:58,260 --> 00:14:00,520
This isn't an oolong highball, right?

162
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:11,560
So pointless...

163
00:14:14,040 --> 00:14:15,079
What's wrong?

164
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:16,080
Did something happen?

165
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:19,580
No idea.

166
00:14:23,230 --> 00:14:25,350
Have you seen Ueno?

167
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:29,340
Who knows.

168
00:14:32,370 --> 00:14:33,370
Ah.

169
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:41,080
Congrats on landing the big client.

170
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:44,960
Thanks...

171
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:55,720
Ueno-san.

172
00:14:55,930 --> 00:14:58,050
- Oh, hey.
- Good work today.

173
00:14:58,690 --> 00:15:01,000
It's rare to see you
at a gathering like this.

174
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:02,400
Yeah.

175
00:15:03,040 --> 00:15:04,400
I'm just here for the free dinner.

176
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:06,390
Same here.

177
00:15:10,540 --> 00:15:11,540
Um...

178
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:14,780
Sorry Shirai is always
giving you a hard time.

179
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:19,880
His epic miscalculations are honestly
kind of impressive at this point.

180
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:22,780
"Epic," huh?

181
00:15:23,660 --> 00:15:25,480
I'm gonna start calling him that.

182
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:35,590
This might be a little out of nowhere,

183
00:15:39,310 --> 00:15:40,820
but I'm actually gay, too.

184
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:43,580
Are you okay?

185
00:15:44,540 --> 00:15:45,630
You didn't know?

186
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:48,360
I'm pretty open about it.

187
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,320
No, it's just...

188
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:52,720
That completely caught me off guard.

189
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:54,410
Sorry about that.

190
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:56,800
It's fine.

191
00:15:57,140 --> 00:15:58,140
I don't really mind.

192
00:15:59,380 --> 00:16:02,470
I heard you were gay too, Ueno-san.

193
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:04,160
Yeah...

194
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:06,360
I see.

195
00:16:08,710 --> 00:16:09,760
Have you told

196
00:16:10,380 --> 00:16:11,580
anyone around you?

197
00:16:13,590 --> 00:16:14,590
No.

198
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:17,260
Just a few people who
joined the company in my year.

199
00:16:17,440 --> 00:16:18,440
Gotcha.

200
00:16:20,460 --> 00:16:21,800
Huh? Kobayashi,

201
00:16:22,220 --> 00:16:23,740
are you and Ueno-san close?

202
00:16:24,230 --> 00:16:26,060
Is there a problem if we are?

203
00:16:26,380 --> 00:16:27,580
I didn't say that.

204
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:31,626
Ueno-san, you and Kanda-san joined
the company in the same year, right?

205
00:16:31,650 --> 00:16:32,770
Wait, how is that, honestly?

206
00:16:32,990 --> 00:16:34,190
Doesn't it feel a bit awkward?

207
00:16:34,950 --> 00:16:37,869
Starting at the same time as
someone as amazing as Kanda-san...

208
00:16:37,870 --> 00:16:39,290
must be really tough on you.

209
00:16:39,820 --> 00:16:42,700
Well, you're in accounting
now, so maybe it doesn't matter.

210
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:45,250
Jeez, stop saying such rude things.

211
00:16:46,020 --> 00:16:47,320
I'm so sorry, Ueno-san.

212
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:49,080
This guy has no filter.

213
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:50,390
It's fine...

214
00:16:50,420 --> 00:16:52,580
Besides, the two of them get along great.

215
00:16:53,140 --> 00:16:54,570
Stop making up your own narrative.

216
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:56,180
Oh, really?

217
00:16:56,200 --> 00:17:00,700
I actually saw them walking
to work together the other day.

218
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,000
That's surprising.

219
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:04,040
I had no idea you two were that close.

220
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:06,780
Sorry for just blurting that out.

221
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:10,580
He just kept making weird
assumptions about you two.

222
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:13,400
- He has a terrible personality. Even before...
- That's not it.

223
00:17:13,490 --> 00:17:14,490
Huh?

224
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:18,340
That was just a coincidence.
He and I aren't particularly close.

225
00:17:19,140 --> 00:17:20,860
It's not like we're on bad terms, though.

226
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:23,700
It's just...

227
00:17:24,600 --> 00:17:27,720
since we started the same year, we
chat occasionally. That's really all it is.

228
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:30,460
It's not like we're best
friends or anything.

229
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:33,260
I see...

230
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:36,589
I'm so sorry for saying such weird things!

231
00:17:36,590 --> 00:17:38,739
- Let's go already!
- See? I knew it was a touchy subject.

232
00:17:38,740 --> 00:17:40,630
Knock it off and let's go!

233
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:50,940
Alright, next stop...

234
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:58,410
the skewer place for round two!

235
00:17:58,740 --> 00:18:01,030
I'm in! I can drink till
sunrise. Who's with me?

236
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:04,290
- Are you going?
- Let's go!

237
00:18:06,420 --> 00:18:08,300
Kanda, you're coming
to the after-party, right?

238
00:18:08,580 --> 00:18:09,580
Oh, sure.

239
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:10,920
I'll be there.

240
00:18:12,340 --> 00:18:13,510
Excuse me.

241
00:18:22,890 --> 00:18:23,890
Found you.

242
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:25,240
Thank goodness.

243
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:31,120
Can I come over to your place now?

244
00:18:31,660 --> 00:18:32,760
Let's have another drink.

245
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:36,860
Oh, right.

246
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:38,280
My bad.

247
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:41,120
Doing things like this
is the problem, isn't it?

248
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:42,660
Huh?

249
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:47,640
I overheard what Nakagawa-san said earlier.

250
00:18:48,860 --> 00:18:50,580
She saw us the other morning, didn't she?

251
00:18:51,820 --> 00:18:52,820
I'm sorry.

252
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:55,220
I'll be more careful from now on.

253
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:03,780
It's not your fault.

254
00:19:06,100 --> 00:19:09,030
I'm just being overly paranoid.

255
00:19:11,230 --> 00:19:12,230
I'm sorry.

256
00:19:15,940 --> 00:19:16,940
I see.

257
00:19:18,980 --> 00:19:21,050
Well, there's a lot to consider.

258
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,870
So, can I still come over?

259
00:19:37,260 --> 00:19:38,260
Sure, you can.

260
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:40,700
What about the after-party, though?

261
00:19:41,360 --> 00:19:42,360
Oh.

262
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:45,400
Everyone's pretty wasted already.
They won't even notice I'm gone.

263
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:48,640
In that case...

264
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:50,560
let's grab some drinks on the way back.

265
00:19:51,350 --> 00:19:52,350
Okay.

266
00:20:06,910 --> 00:20:08,800
The night breeze feels so nice.

267
00:20:15,980 --> 00:20:16,980
Oh!

268
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:18,460
Let's have hot pot next time.

269
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:21,066
Since we went to the
trouble of buying that pot.

270
00:20:21,090 --> 00:20:22,360
I'm craving offal hot pot.

271
00:20:23,740 --> 00:20:25,960
What kind do you want, Ueno?

272
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:46,560
Well...

273
00:20:48,370 --> 00:20:49,370
Wait, if...

274
00:20:50,300 --> 00:20:52,060
- If it's a bother for you...
- Kanda.

275
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:03,260
Here.

276
00:21:05,260 --> 00:21:06,260
Huh?

277
00:21:06,850 --> 00:21:07,850
A congratulatory gift.

278
00:21:18,840 --> 00:21:21,000
I was going to wait until
your promotion was official.

279
00:21:21,660 --> 00:21:22,780
But I was afraid I'd forget.

280
00:21:22,920 --> 00:21:25,176
Or one of us might suddenly
get transferred or something.

281
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:26,720
Just sell it if you don't want it.

282
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:30,200
You don't have to use it...

283
00:21:35,670 --> 00:21:36,670
Wait...

284
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,160
You're opening it right here?

285
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:41,260
It's a tie...

286
00:21:45,540 --> 00:21:48,160
That's what you get for sending
me such a half-hearted wishlist.

287
00:21:49,360 --> 00:21:51,240
So I just picked one based on my own taste.

288
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:56,060
I don't know what people
usually go for, so don't complain.

289
00:22:02,040 --> 00:22:03,040
Ueno...

290
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:07,260
Thank you.

291
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:09,600
I'm so happy.

292
00:22:17,200 --> 00:22:18,250
Well? How is it?

293
00:22:19,920 --> 00:22:20,920
Does it look good?

294
00:22:23,380 --> 00:22:24,380
Yeah.

295
00:22:26,300 --> 00:22:27,820
Sorry I just went with my own taste...

296
00:22:28,960 --> 00:22:31,320
You picked it out, Ueno,
so I know it looks great.

297
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:33,260
Oh, but...

298
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:36,780
I still want to see how
it looks in the mirror.

299
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:39,500
Let's hurry back.

300
00:22:40,680 --> 00:22:41,680
Yeah.

301
00:22:44,560 --> 00:22:45,560
Let's go.

302
00:22:46,150 --> 00:22:47,790
I want to see the happy look on his face.

303
00:22:49,200 --> 00:22:53,860
Because he works so hard every day, I want to
give him something special from time to time.

304
00:22:57,080 --> 00:22:58,180
Moments like these...

305
00:22:58,920 --> 00:23:00,180
more than anyone else...

306
00:23:00,960 --> 00:23:02,960
I want to be the one he
shares them with the most.

307
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:20,150
There I go again...

308
00:24:14,780 --> 00:24:17,030
(Next Episode Preview)
What do I even want anymore?

309
00:24:17,380 --> 00:24:19,760
Isn't being able to sleep
together the first hurdle?

310
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:21,490
You're not even my type.

311
00:24:21,670 --> 00:24:24,280
Nothing is ever going to happen between us.

312
00:24:24,700 --> 00:24:28,580
I guess that's what you'd
call friends with benefits.
